@775 = ~Ultimate Dispelling Field~
@776 = ~Ultimate Dispelling Field (Abjuration)
Level: 7
Range: 0
Duration: special
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: 10-meter radius
Saving Throw: none

This spell is a more powerful version of Dispelling Field, which acts the same way, but treating the caster's level as doubled. Thus, if a level 16 warlord casts this spell, it dispels magic of all creatures within 10-meter radius as if he were level 32.
Whatever the result, there is always at least 1% chance of success or failure.~
@7761 = ~Ultimate Dispelling Field (Abjuration)
Level: 7
Range: 0
Duration: special
Casting Time: 3
Area of Effect: 10-meter radius
Saving Throw: none

This spell is a more powerful version of Dispelling Field, which acts the same way, but treating the caster's level as doubled. Thus, when the warlord casts this spell, it dispels magic of all creatures within 10-meter radius as if he were level 40.
Whatever the result, there is always at least 1% chance of success or failure.~

@777 = ~Wrath of the Earth~
@778 = ~Wrath of the Earth (Alteration)
Level: 7
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 1 round
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: special

This spell unleashes all the power of earth against a single creature. When this spell is cast, the earth's forces converge to open a seismic fissure beneath the target.
If the target makes a successful save vs. spell, the fissure is limited and spits out a tongue of fire dealing 10D6 points of damage.
But if the target fails the saving throw, the fissure is significant enough for the creature to fall into it. The victim suffers an additional 10D10 points of slashing damage when the fissure closes and must make a save vs. breath weapon at -2 to avoid dying crushed. If he succeeds this second saving throw, he is only partly crushed and is left severely impaired (-4 to AC and to hit, movement speed reduced by half).~
@7781 = ~Crushed by the Fissure~
@7782 = ~Wrath of the Earth (Alteration)
Level: 7
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 1 round
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: special

This spell unleashes all the power of earth against a single creature. When this spell is cast, the earth's forces converge to open a seismic fissure beneath the target.
If the target makes a successful save vs. spell, the fissure is limited and spits out a tongue of fire dealing 10D6 points of damage.
But if the target fails the saving throw, the fissure is significant enough for the creature to fall into it. The victim suffers an additional 10D10 points of slashing damage when the fissure closes and must make a save vs. breath weapon at -2 to avoid dying crushed. If he succeeds this second saving throw, he is only partly crushed and is left severely impaired (-4 to AC and to hit, movement speed reduced by half).~
@7781 = ~Crushed by the Fissure~

@779 = ~Major Disorder~
@7710 = ~Major Disorder (Enchantment)
Level: 7
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: special
Casting Time: 7
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: special

Major Disorder inflicts devastating cerebral trauma on the target. If it fails a saving throw, it is driven mad and left in a permanent vegetative state. Only a spell of Greater Restoration or Wish can cure this condition. If the saving throw is successful, it will still remain confused for 2 turns.~
@77101 = ~Major Disorder (Enchantment)
Level: 7
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: special
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: special

Major Disorder inflicts devastating cerebral trauma on the target. If it fails a saving throw, it is driven mad and left in a permanent vegetative state. Only a spell of Greater Restoration or Wish can cure this condition. If the saving throw is successful, it will still remain confused for 2 turns.~

@7711 = ~Devastation~
@7712 = ~Devastation (Necromancy, Abjuration)
Level: 7
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 2 rounds / level
Casting Time: 6
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: special

This spell aims to drastically reduce the resistance of an exceptionally powerful creature.
It acts in several stages:
First, it reduces magic resistance of the target by 20%. There is no saving throw allowed against this, and the initial magic resistance of the creature does not protect it at all.
Then, if the spell isn't negated by the remaining magic resistance of the creature, it suffers a -4 penalty to all saving throws. Again, there is no saving throw allowed to resist.
Finally, if the creature fails a save vs. spell, it will suffer the following penalties:
- 4 to AC
Strength and constitution set at 8
- 30% elemental damage resistance
- 20% physical damage resistance

If the creature has no initial resistance to damage or elements, this becomes a vulnerability.

The penalties increase with the warlord's experience, according to the following table:
Level 15: strength and constitution set at 5
Level 16: AC reduction set to -6
Level 17: elemental resistance reduction set to -50%
Level 18: physical resistance reduction set to -35%
Level 19: magic resistance reduction set to -30%
Level 20: saving throws reduction set to -6
Level 21: shock inflicted by the spell in case of a failed saving throw is so powerful that if the creature has fewer than 60 hit points, it will die.

If the spell is cast several times on a creature, it can stack according to the following table:
Spell negated by magic resistance: magic resistance reduction of the following spell is cumulative.
Spell negated by a successful saving throw: magic resistance reduction and saving throws reduction of the following spell are cumulative.
Failed saving throw: the target suffers the full effects and cannot be affected again for the duration of the spell.~
@77129 = ~Vulnerability Increased~
@771291 = ~Devastation (Necromancy, Abjuration)
Level: 7
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 4 turns
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: special

This spell aims to drastically reduce the resistance of an exceptionally powerful creature.
It acts in several stages:
First, it reduces magic resistance of the target by 30%. There is no saving throw allowed against this, and the initial magic resistance of the creature does not protect it at all.
Then, if the spell isn't negated by the remaining magic resistance of the creature, it suffers a -6 penalty to all saving throws. Again, there is no saving throw allowed to resist.
Finally, if the creature fails a save vs. spell, it will suffer the following penalties:
- 6 to AC
Strength and constitution set at 5
- 50% elemental damage resistance
- 35% physical damage resistance

If the creature has no initial resistance to damage or elements, this becomes a vulnerability.

At level 21, shock inflicted by the spell in case of a failed saving throw is so powerful that if the creature has fewer than 60 hit points, it will die.

If the spell is cast several times on a creature, it can stack according to the following table:
Spell negated by magic resistance: magic resistance reduction of the following spell is cumulative.
Spell negated by a successful saving throw: magic resistance reduction and saving throws reduction of the following spell are cumulative.
Failed saving throw: the target suffers the full effects and cannot be affected again for the duration of the spell.~

@7713 = ~Energy in All~
@7714 = ~Energy in All (Alteration, Enchantment)
Level: 7
Range: 0
Duration: 1 round / 3 levels
Casting Time: 9
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

The warlord tried to create this spell from a simple principle: "If magic is present in all things, I have to take advantage of it". And the spell works, but randomly, because the Weave is difficult to manipulate without years of study.
The spell allows the warlord to absorb the surrounding magic to restore his own magic, allowing him to recall spells he has already cast.
Each round, the mage will remember a spell of level 1 to 8 (determined by rolling a d8; it is not possible to recall a spell of level 9 that way). But he must be careful: every bit of magic that the body of the mage absorbs can hurt him. Every time he remembers a spell, the mage must make a successful save vs. death (at a -1 penalty for level 4-6 spells and -2 for spells of levels 7 and 8) or suffer 1 point of damage per level of the recalled spell from the resulting magical discharge.
There is also a 20% chance, reduced by 1% for every 2 caster levels, (minimum 10% at level 20) at every cast of the spell that the attempt to control the Weave fails, causing the opposite of the desired effect: the spellcaster has his magic absorbed by the Weave and forgets 1D10 spells.~
@77141 = ~Energy in All (Alteration, Enchantment)
Level: 7
Range: 0
Duration: 6 rounds (7 at level 21)
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

